## Story
Alice is working on a project that involves analyzing data represented in a square matrix format. As part of her analysis, she needs to determine if the sum of the diagonal elements in the matrix is perfectly divisible by the sum of the boundary elements. She seeks your help to write a program that can efficiently perform this check.

## Problem
Given a square matrix (2D array), you need to calculate the sum of all elements present on both diagonals (primary and secondary). Also, calculate the sum of elements present on the boundary of the matrix. Your task is to determine if the diagonal sum is divisible by the boundary sum. If it is, return "YES"; otherwise, return "NO".

## Input Format
The first line contains an integer N, representing the number of rows and columns of the square matrix.
The next N lines contain N space-separated integers, representing the elements of the matrix.

## Output Format
Print "YES" if the sum of the diagonal elements is divisible by the sum of the boundary elements. Otherwise, print "NO".

## Constraints
* 1 <= N <= 100, where N is the number of rows/columns in the square matrix.
* 1 <= matrix[i][j] <= 1000
* Matrix is always a square matrix (N x N).
* The matrix will always have at least one element (N >= 1).

## Pseudocode
```
function isDivisible(matrix):
n = size of matrix
diagonalSum = 0
boundarySum = 0

// Calculate diagonal sum
for i from 0 to n-1:
diagonalSum = diagonalSum + matrix[i][i]  // Primary diagonal
diagonalSum = diagonalSum + matrix[i][n-1-i] // Secondary diagonal
if n is odd:
diagonalSum = diagonalSum - matrix[n/2][n/2] //Subtract the center element as it will be added twice for odd sized matrices.

// Calculate boundary sum
for i from 0 to n-1:
for j from 0 to n-1:
if i == 0 or i == n-1 or j == 0 or j == n-1:
boundarySum = boundarySum + matrix[i][j]

//Check if boundary sum is zero
if boundarySum == 0:
return "NO"

// Check if diagonal sum is divisible by boundary sum
if diagonalSum is divisible by boundarySum:
return "YES"
else:
return "NO"
