return i

if arr[0] > 0:
return n

return n + 1
```

## Story
Alice is learning about number theory and matrices in her math class. Her teacher gave her a square matrix of integers as homework and asked her to determine if the product of all the elements in the matrix is divisible by the cube of the sum of the digits of all the elements in the matrix. Alice finds this task quite tedious and asks for your help.

## Problem
Given a square matrix of integers, your task is to check if the product of all the elements in the matrix is divisible by the cube of the sum of the digits of all the elements in the matrix.
Specifically, calculate the product of all the elements in the input matrix. Also, calculate the sum of the digits of all elements in the matrix. Check if the product is divisible by the cube of the digit sum. If it is divisible, print "YES". Otherwise, print "NO".

## Input Format
The first line contains an integer N, representing the number of rows and columns in the square matrix.
The next N lines each contain N space-separated integers representing the elements of the matrix.

## Output Format
Print "YES" if the product of the elements in the matrix is divisible by the cube of the sum of the digits of all the elements. Otherwise, print "NO".

## Constraints
* 1 <= N <= 10 (where N is the number of rows/columns in the matrix)
* 1 <= matrix[i][j] <= 100
* The matrix contains only non-negative integers.

